        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: Battle of Kircholm, Polish–Swedish War (1600–11)\n- Places: Livonia, Estonia\n- People: Charles IX of Sweden, Sigismund III of Poland\n- Topics: control of Livonia and Estonia, dispute over the Swedish throne\n\nFacts:\n- The Polish–Swedish War (1600–11) was a continuation of the struggle between Sweden and Poland over control of Livonia and Estonia and over the Swedish throne.\n- The dispute over the Swedish throne in the Polish–Swedish War involved Charles IX of Sweden and Sigismund III of Poland.\n- The Battle of Kircholm took place on 27 September 1605, or 17 September in the Old Style calendar used in Protestant countries.\n- The Battle of Kircholm was one of the major battles in the Polish–Swedish War.",
